## Title: Daseeki Bags 2 (BETA)
## Notes: A standalone bag interface for WoW Classic Era.
## Author: Daseeki
## Category: Bags & Inventory
## X-License: MIT
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1592410
## OptionalDeps: Daseeki-Core, Daseeki-Nexus
## Interface: 11507, 11508, 11509
## Version: 2.0.0
## SavedVariables: DaseekiBags2DB, DaseekiBags2Data, DaseekiBagsAccount, DaseekiBagsSets, DaseekiBagsMesh
##
## Daseeki-Bags 2.0 — clean rewrite. This toc documents the intended 2.0
## load order for the fresh flat tree; it is NOT wired into the live addon yet
## (the shipping Daseeki-Bags.toc still loads the 1.x tree). Cutover in a later
## wave replaces Daseeki-Bags.toc with this file and deletes the 1.x sources.
##
## SAVEDVARIABLES CONTRACT (ROLLOUT_CONTINUITY_AUDIT AT-RISK-1 — the cutover's
## most destructive defect, and the reason all FIVE globals are declared here):
## the client rewrites this addon's SavedVariables file at every logout from the
## DECLARED names only. Any global not listed above is simply not written back —
## so the moment a 2.0 toc that declares only the 2.0 pair replaces the 1.x toc,
## the three 1.x globals are erased at the first logout, silently and for good.
## Migration would get exactly ONE attempt and rollback would be impossible.
##
## 2.0 therefore DECLARES the 1.x trio while never writing it: migrate.lua and
## migrate_settings.lua read it READ-ONLY. Declaring it keeps it on disk as a
## rollback net, so a partial or failed import can re-run on a later login and
## the owner can downgrade to 1.x with data intact.
##
## KEEP ALL FIVE DECLARED FOR AT LEAST 2 RELEASES AFTER CUTOVER. Dropping a 1.x
## name from this line deletes that data at the very next logout.
##   DaseekiBags2DB     — 2.0 settings (schema-versioned)
##   DaseekiBags2Data   — 2.0 inventory cache DB (owners graph; per-container identity)
##   DaseekiBagsAccount — 1.x full per-character bag data   (read-only source)
##   DaseekiBagsSets    — 1.x settings + custom rules       (read-only source)
##   DaseekiBagsMesh    — 1.x cross-account summaries       (read-only source)
##
core.lua
store.lua
# nexus.lua: the SOFT-REQUIRED Daseeki-Nexus Inventory bridge. Bags sources its SUMMARY
# owners (the money tooltip's "Other Accounts" section and the cross-character tooltip
# counts) from the Nexus owners graph when that module is present and populated, and
# defers migrate.lua's DaseekiBagsMesh import to it. ZERO hard dependency: every call is
# type-guarded and falls back to Bags' own store, so the addon is unchanged without
# Nexus. Daseeki-Nexus is on the OptionalDeps line above for LOAD ORDER only -- so its
# SavedVariables are attached before our ADDON_LOADED runs Store.Init -> Migrate.Migrate
# and the deferral decision can see them. We never declare its globals here: declaring
# another addon's SavedVariables would make both addons write the same file.
# Loads after store.lua (it builds store-shaped owner records); every consumer resolves
# ns.Nexus at call time, so its position relative to them is free.
nexus.lua
capture.lua
migrate.lua
# migrate_settings.lua: the 1.x SETTINGS + custom-rules pass (audit NW-1), run at
# the same migration moment as migrate.lua's owner pass (migrate.Migrate calls it).
# Separate file because it converts DaseekiBagsSets, a different source with a
# different marker, and it consumes the search grammar at CALL time (not load time),
# so its position here is free.
migrate_settings.lua
# --- W2 (UI) --- loads after Daseeki-Core (OptionalDeps) so DaseekiUI exists ---
borders.lua
ui_items.lua
# parity.lua: the CELL-PARITY GATE. A line-cited transcription of what Daseeki-Bags 1.x
# draws in one bag cell, kept next to what 2.0 draws, with an assertion on every row. It
# exists to stop the "the grid still reads cluttered" loop becoming a fourth round of
# guessing: any per-cell element that drifts from the 1.x model turns the suite red and
# names the row. Pure Lua, no frames; loads after ui_items so both models are resolvable.
parity.lua
ui_frame.lua
ui_owner.lua
ui_bank.lua
# --- W4 (search / sort / options) --- pure engines + DaseekiUI settings page ---
search.lua
# rules2 (W4.5): simplified custom-categories engine (a category = a saved search
# query; reuses the search.lua matcher). Consumed by ui_frame (combined-view category
# SECTIONS) and options.lua (the editor). MUST load — without it ns.Rules is nil, so
# Frame.CategoriesEnabled() is false and the combined view falls back to a flat grid
# with zero section headers (was the missing-categories beta defect). After search.lua
# (its matcher), before options.lua (the editor consumes ns.Rules).
rules2.lua
sort.lua
ui_find.lua
options.lua
features.lua
#
# Bindings.xml is deliberately NOT listed here. The client auto-discovers
# Bindings.xml at the addon root and hands it to the KEYBINDINGS parser. Listing
# it as a .toc file entry ALSO feeds it to the generic UI-XML parser, which does
# not know the <Binding> element -- that is what produced the LUA_WARNINGs the
# owner saw on every load ("Unrecognized XML: Binding", "Unrecognized XML
# attribute: header/category"). No shipping Era addon lists Bindings.xml in its
# .toc, and 1.x never did either. Do not re-add it.
#
# Corollary: because discovery is per FOLDER and by file name, this .toc cannot
# suppress Bindings.xml either. If any second installed folder also ships a
# Bindings.xml with the DASEEKIBAGS2_* names, the client logs "Binding
# DASEEKIBAGS2_TOGGLE was attempted to be loaded more than once" against the
# second folder. That is an install-topology defect (e.g. the repo checkout
# junctioned in as the live 1.x addon while on a v2 branch), not a .toc defect.
